; Benchmark 18: a very large pattern (10 000 features).
;
; Task: a 200 x 200 x 2 perforated screen with a 100 x 100 grid of 1.2 mm
; holes on a 2 mm pitch: 10 000 holes. Build it two ways and check they
; agree:
;   explicit: pattern-linear of pattern-linear (a min over 10 000 cylinders)
;   periodic: one hole, repeated with repeat-x / repeat-y (mod), clipped to
;             the hole field's extent
; Also: 10 000 pin instances in the holes, as an assembly (generated by
; the benchmark's test, b18 in crates/ink-cli/tests/cli/benchmarks.rs:
; instances cannot be generated in IR).
;
; Reference: V = 200 x 200 x 2 - 10000 pi 0.6^2 2 = 57 380.5 mm^3
;
; Pass criteria (each command < 60 s):
;   - ink check of the explicit version;
;   - both volumes within 0.5% of 57 380.5;
;   - both mesh watertight (at res 0.25: 8 cells across a hole);
;   - the 10 000-pin assembly: interfere finds no collision.

(import "std")

(param n 100)            ; holes per side (load-time)
(param pitch 2)
(param hole-r 0.6)
(def plate (box 200 200 2))
(def x0 (* -0.5 pitch (- n 1)))
(def hole (move (cylinder-z hole-r 10) x0 x0 0))
(def holes-explicit (pattern-linear (pattern-linear hole n pitch 0 0) n 0 pitch 0))
(body screen-explicit (shape (subtract plate holes-explicit)) (attr color "#888888"))

; periodic version: the lattice of holes, limited to the n x n block.
; repeat-x/-y put copies at multiples of the period around the origin, so
; the lattice is shifted to x0 (the first version had every hole 1 mm off:
; its volume matched, and only the pin assembly's interfere caught it).
(def holes-periodic
  (max (move (repeat-x (repeat-y (cylinder-z hole-r 10) pitch) pitch) x0 x0 0)
       (- (max (abs x) (abs y)) (* 0.5 pitch n))))
(body screen-periodic (shape (subtract plate holes-periodic)) (attr color "#888888"))
